# GATE-K8REACH registry — every UNAOS_* knob with no K8_FEATS arm, and why.
# NA <reason> = deliberately absent from the Pi bare-metal image.
# TODO <owner/note> = grandfathered at seeding, nobody has ruled yet.
# `scripts/k8-reach.py --evidence <KNOB>` prints the sites behind a row.
#
# AN `NA` ROW CITES THE COMMAND THAT JUSTIFIED IT, not a reason string alone (pi 7,
# 2026-09-06). A human first pass inherits the classifier's blind spots exactly: the
# arch-neutral file (`nvidia-kepler`'s site in `video/wm.rs`) and the x86-gated callee
# (`rastmc`) are the cases a reader also mis-sorts, because the path and the cfg both
# look decisive and neither is. `NA  x86 only` is a second classifier with no proof and
# worse recall; `NA  --evidence: 11 sites, 0 Pi-live (all under drivers/gpu, x86 mod tree)`
# is checkable by the next seat.
UNAOS_BAR1EXP              TODO  seeded 2026-09-06; no Pi-live cfg site
UNAOS_BCMARECON            TODO  seeded 2026-09-06; no Pi-live cfg site
UNAOS_BCMAS1               TODO  seeded 2026-09-06; no Pi-live cfg site
UNAOS_BEAM   NA   --evidence: beam 12 sites 11 Pi-live 1 NEG [implies: jd1dc]; Cargo.toml `beam = ["jd1dc"]` (the guard and the aperture are that rung's; UNAOS_JD1DC is the TODO row above). Ten of the eleven Pi-live sites are in arch/aarch64/display_tegra.rs, a module declared `#[cfg(feature = "tegra")] pub mod display_tegra` (arch/aarch64/mod.rs:111) — a Pi image never lexes the file; the eleventh is arch/aarch64/mod.rs:562, conjoined `all(feature = "tegra", feature = "beam")`, whose `not(...)` twin is the NEG. The consumer, video/beam.rs, is unconditional and arch-neutral on purpose (it is the MECHANISM, not a knob site) and folds to a no-op wherever `arch::scanout_beam()` is the constant `None` — which on the Pi it is: the BCM2711 HVS publishes no raster-line register this kernel reads, so there is nothing for the knob to arm there. The register it locks is Tegra234 nvdisplay `NV_PDISP_RG_DPCA` under the display@ BPMP power guard.
